+/**
+ * Refuse to hand out BIP360 P2MR receiving addresses on a chain where the deployment is disabled.
+ *
+ * Where P2MR never activates, a 32 byte witness v2 program is just an unknown witness program:
+ * consensus accepts any witness for it, so coins paid to such an address can be taken by the first
+ * miner that notices. Entry points that produce addresses meant for receiving must not offer them
+ * there. Parsing and inspection (getdescriptorinfo) stay available.
+ *
+ * @param[in] scripts The scriptPubKeys a descriptor produces.
+ * @throws JSONRPCError if any of them is a P2MR output and P2MR is disabled on this chain.
+ */
+void CheckP2MRReceiveAllowed(std::span<const CScript> scripts);
